---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import WindowFrame from '../components/calculator/WindowFrame.astro';

const canonicalUrl = 'https://calcumetrics.com/methodology';

const jsonld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      name: 'Methodology: Financial Engineering, Formulas & Statutory Conventions',
      url: canonicalUrl,
      description: 'Transparent mathematical formulas, statutory conventions, worked test fixture proofs, and regulatory data sources governing Calcumetrics calculators.',
      publisher: { '@id': 'https://calcumetrics.com/#org' },
      dateModified: '2026-09-24',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://calcumetrics.com/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Methodology', item: canonicalUrl },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="Methodology: Financial Formulas & Proofs | Calcumetrics"
  description="Transparent mathematical formulas, statutory conventions, worked test fixture proofs, and regulatory data sources governing Calcumetrics calculators."
  canonical={canonicalUrl}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonld)} />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6">
      <ol class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-text-muted">
        <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-accent transition-standard">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-hidden="true">›</li>
        <li class="text-text-primary font-medium" aria-current="page">Methodology</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2 flex-wrap">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-accent/10 text-accent">
          Mathematical Transparency
        </span>
        <span class="text-xs text-text-muted">Last updated: 24 September 2026</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-text-muted">·</span>
        <a href="/about#corrections-log" class="text-xs text-accent hover:underline font-medium">
          View Corrections Log →
        </a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-text-primary mb-4">
        Methodology: Plain-Language Principles, Formulas &amp; Statutory Conventions
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Financial tools should never be black boxes. Whether you are a commerce student cross-checking an examination problem, a Chartered Accountant auditing a loan schedule, or an everyday investor planning a retirement corpus, you have a right to inspect the exact math, conventions, and regulatory baselines behind your results.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Layout: Main Content + Sticky "On this page" Sidebar -->
    <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10 items-start">
      
      <!-- Main Content (8 cols) -->
      <main class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-12 min-w-0">

        <!-- 1. Interactive Live Sandbox -->
        <section id="sandbox" class="scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="sandbox-heading">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
            <h2 id="sandbox-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary">
              Live Calculation Engine Simulator
            </h2>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800">
              100% In-Browser Memory
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mb-4 leading-relaxed">
            Drag the sliders below. Notice how the calculation executes continuously in your local browser memory with zero network delay and zero server roundtrips.
          </p>

          <WindowFrame variant="dark" urlPill="calcumetrics.com/methodology#sandbox">
            <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 text-dark-text">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-dark-border pb-3 mb-5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-pulse"></span>
                  <span class="text-xs font-bold text-dark-accent uppercase tracking-wider">Live Math Sandbox</span>
                </div>
                <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-dark-muted hidden sm:inline">Execution: 0 Server Calls</span>
              </div>

              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 items-start">
                <!-- Col 1: INPUT -->
                <div class="space-y-3.5">
                  <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-dark-muted flex items-center gap-1.5">
                    <span>1. Input (Local State)</span>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <label for="demo-principal" class="text-xs text-dark-muted mb-1 flex justify-between">
                      <span>Principal (P)</span>
                      <span id="demo-principal-val" class="font-mono text-dark-text font-bold tabular-nums">₹5,00,000</span>
                    </label>
                    <input
                      type="range"
                      id="demo-principal"
                      min="50000"
                      max="2500000"
                      step="25000"
                      value="500000"
                      class="w-full h-2 bg-dark-border rounded-control appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-dark-accent py-2"
                      aria-label="Demo Principal Amount"
                    />
                  </div>

                  <div>
                    <label for="demo-rate" class="text-xs text-dark-muted mb-1 flex justify-between">
                      <span>Annual Rate (r)</span>
                      <span id="demo-rate-val" class="font-mono text-dark-text font-bold tabular-nums">7.5%</span>
                    </label>
                    <input
                      type="range"
                      id="demo-rate"
                      min="1"
                      max="15"
                      step="0.25"
                      value="7.5"
                      class="w-full h-2 bg-dark-border rounded-control appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-dark-accent py-2"
                      aria-label="Demo Annual Interest Rate"
                    />
                  </div>

                  <div class="text-[11px] text-dark-muted flex justify-between pt-1 border-t border-dark-border/40">
                    <span>Tenure (t)</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-dark-text font-medium">5 years (annual compounding)</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Col 2: ENGINE -->
                <div>
                  <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-dark-muted mb-3.5 flex items-center gap-1.5">
                    <span>2. Mathematical Engine</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="bg-surface/5 border border-dark-border rounded-control p-3.5 font-mono text-xs space-y-2">
                    <div class="text-dark-muted text-[11px] font-sans font-medium">Standard Equation:</div>
                    <div class="text-dark-accent font-semibold">A = P × (1 + r)ᵗ</div>
                    <div class="text-dark-muted text-[11px] pt-1.5 border-t border-dark-border font-sans font-medium">Live In-Memory Step:</div>
                    <div id="demo-engine-calc" class="text-dark-text text-[11px] break-all tabular-nums font-mono leading-relaxed">
                      500000 × (1 + 0.075)⁵
                    </div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] text-dark-muted pt-1 border-t border-dark-border font-sans">
                      Floating Point: IEEE 754 64-bit precision
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Col 3: OUTPUT -->
                <div>
                  <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-dark-muted mb-3.5 flex items-center gap-1.5">
                    <span>3. Reactive Output</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="bg-surface/5 border border-dark-border rounded-control p-3.5 flex flex-col justify-between min-h-[145px]">
                    <div>
                      <div class="text-[11px] text-dark-muted uppercase font-semibold">Maturity Corpus (A)</div>
                      <div id="demo-output-result" class="text-2xl font-extrabold tabular-nums text-dark-accent mt-1 tracking-tight">
                        ₹7,17,815
                      </div>
                      <div id="demo-output-gain" class="text-xs text-dark-text font-medium tabular-nums mt-1">
                        + ₹2,17,815 wealth gain
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pt-2 border-t border-dark-border flex items-center justify-between text-[10px] text-dark-muted">
                      <span>Display format:</span>
                      <span class="text-dark-text font-mono font-medium">Indian Lakhs/Crores</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </WindowFrame>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. Core Engineering Principles -->
        <section id="principles" class="scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
          <h2 id="principles-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">
            Core Engineering &amp; Architectural Standards
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-5 leading-relaxed">
            Our technical choices are intentionally conservative. In financial calculation, predictability and accuracy supersede flashy dependencies.
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <!-- 1. No Server Calls -->
            <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 space-y-2">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary">No Server Calls</h3>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800 font-semibold">100% Client-Side</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Calculations execute entirely in your local browser JavaScript engine. We never transmit your income, loan balances, or investment amounts to a backend server or third-party API.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- 2. Continuous Statutory Audits -->
            <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 space-y-2">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary">Continuous Statutory Audits</h3>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400 border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800 font-semibold">Event-Driven</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
                We do not rely on passive annual audits. When statutory changes occur mid-year (such as the September 2025 GST 2.0 rate rationalization or Finance Act amendments), models and test suites are updated and deployed immediately.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- 3. IEEE 754 Float & Rounding Drift -->
            <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 space-y-2">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary">Strict Precision Boundaries</h3>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-canvas text-text-muted border border-border font-semibold">IEEE 754 64-bit</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Computers store binary decimals with small approximations. Calcumetrics preserves full unrounded floating-point precision throughout all multi-step iterations (e.g. 240-month amortization schedules), rounding strictly at the final display step.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- 4. Immutable Mathematical Formulas -->
            <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 space-y-2">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary">Immutable Proofs</h3>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-canvas text-text-muted border border-border font-semibold">Automated CI/CD</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Formulas never silently change. Every calculator engine is anchored by rigorous unit test fixtures verified in automated CI/CD pipelines before any code is published.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 3. Master Formulas & Plain-Language Explanations -->
        <section id="formulas" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6" aria-labelledby="formulas-heading">
          <div>
            <h2 id="formulas-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">
              Master Formulas &amp; Statutory Specifications
            </h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
              Below are the exact mathematical models and statutory conventions implemented across Calcumetrics. Every formula is rendered with native browser MathML and links directly to its live calculator.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Formula: SIP -->
          <article id="sip" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap">
              <div>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Investments · Compounding</span>
                <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">
                  1. Systematic Investment Plan (SIP) — Annuity-Due Model
                </h3>
              </div>
              <a href="/sip-calculator" class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">
                Try SIP Calculator →
              </a>
            </div>

            <!-- Plain explanation -->
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Plain-Language Explanation:</strong> In an equity SIP, bank auto-debits debit your installment on a scheduled day at the <em>beginning</em> of each monthly cycle. Because each month's installment earns compounding growth from day one of that month, the calculation requires an <strong>annuity-due</strong> formula rather than a standard end-of-month annuity.
            </p>

            <!-- Native MathML Equation -->
            <div class="p-4 bg-canvas border border-border rounded-control overflow-x-auto text-center" aria-label="SIP Annuity-Due Equation">
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" class="text-base sm:text-lg text-accent font-semibold py-1">
                <mi>M</mi>
                <mo>=</mo>
                <mi>P</mi>
                <mo>×</mo>
                <mfrac>
                  <mrow>
                    <msup>
                      <mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow>
                      <mi>n</mi>
                    </msup>
                    <mo>−</mo>
                    <mn>1</mn>
                  </mrow>
                  <mi>i</mi>
                </mfrac>
                <mo>×</mo>
                <mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow>
              </math>
              <span class="sr-only">M = P * [((1 + i)^n - 1) / i] * (1 + i)</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Details toggle -->
            <details class="text-xs text-text-muted border-t border-border pt-3 cursor-pointer group">
              <summary class="font-semibold text-text-primary hover:text-accent select-none list-none flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>View Mathematical Variables &amp; Assumptions</span>
                <span class="text-accent group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2 pl-2">
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">M</strong> = Estimated Future Value (Total Maturity Corpus)</div>
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">P</strong> = Monthly investment amount</div>
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">i</strong> = Monthly compounding rate = Annual Rate ÷ 12 ÷ 100</div>
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">n</strong> = Total number of monthly installments (Years × 12)</div>
              </div>
            </details>
          </article>

          <!-- Formula: EMI -->
          <article id="emi" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap">
              <div>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Loans · Amortization</span>
                <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">
                  2. Equated Monthly Installment (EMI) — Reducing Balance
                </h3>
              </div>
              <a href="/emi-calculator" class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">
                Try EMI Calculator →
              </a>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Plain-Language Explanation:</strong> In a genuine reducing-balance loan (standard for Indian home, car, and personal loans under RBI guidelines), your interest for month <em>t</em> is calculated solely on the remaining unpaid loan principal, not on the original sanction amount. As principal decreases with each installment, the interest portion of your EMI shrinks while the principal reduction portion grows.
            </p>

            <div class="p-4 bg-canvas border border-border rounded-control overflow-x-auto text-center" aria-label="EMI Equation">
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" class="text-base sm:text-lg text-accent font-semibold py-1">
                <mi>E</mi>
                <mo>=</mo>
                <mfrac>
                  <mrow>
                    <mi>P</mi>
                    <mo>×</mo>
                    <mi>r</mi>
                    <mo>×</mo>
                    <msup>
                      <mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow>
                      <mi>n</mi>
                    </msup>
                  </mrow>
                  <mrow>
                    <msup>
                      <mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow>
                      <mi>n</mi>
                    </msup>
                    <mo>−</mo>
                    <mn>1</mn>
                  </mrow>
                </mfrac>
              </math>
              <span class="sr-only">E = [P * r * (1 + r)^n] / [((1 + r)^n) - 1]</span>
            </div>

            <details class="text-xs text-text-muted border-t border-border pt-3 cursor-pointer group">
              <summary class="font-semibold text-text-primary hover:text-accent select-none list-none flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>View Mathematical Variables &amp; RBI Compliance</span>
                <span class="text-accent group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2 pl-2">
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">E</strong> = Equated Monthly Installment</div>
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">P</strong> = Loan principal sanction amount</div>
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">r</strong> = Monthly rate = Annual Rate ÷ 12 ÷ 100</div>
                <div><strong class="text-text-primary font-mono">n</strong> = Total tenure in months (Years × 12)</div>
              </div>
            </details>
          </article>

          <!-- Formula: GST 2.0 -->
          <article id="gst" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap">
              <div>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Taxation · Indirect Tax</span>
                <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">
                  3. Goods &amp; Services Tax (GST 2.0 Reform)
                </h3>
              </div>
              <a href="/in/gst-calculator" class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">
                Try GST Calculator →
              </a>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Plain-Language Explanation:</strong> Following the landmark GST Council rate rationalization effective September 2025, India transitioned to a modern 4-slab architecture (0% Nil, 5% Merit, 18% Standard, 40% Luxury/Demerit), phasing out the former 12% and 28% slabs. Calcumetrics calculates forward exclusive tax and reverse inclusive tax extraction with exact split into equal CGST and SGST halves (or IGST for interstate).
            </p>

            <div class="p-4 bg-canvas border border-border rounded-control overflow-x-auto text-center" aria-label="GST Equations">
              <div class="space-y-3">
                <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" class="text-sm sm:text-base text-accent font-semibold">
                  <mtext>Exclusive (Add GST):&#160;</mtext>
                  <mtext>Tax</mtext>
                  <mo>=</mo>
                  <mfrac>
                    <mrow><mtext>Net Price</mtext><mo>×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow>
                    <mn>100</mn>
                  </mfrac>
                </math>
                <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" class="text-sm sm:text-base text-accent font-semibold">
                  <mtext>Inclusive (Extract GST):&#160;</mtext>
                  <mtext>Tax</mtext>
                  <mo>=</mo>
                  <mtext>Gross Price</mtext>
                  <mo>−</mo>
                  <mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>Gross Price</mtext><mo>×</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow>
                </math>
              </div>
            </div>

            <details class="text-xs text-text-muted border-t border-border pt-3 cursor-pointer group">
              <summary class="font-semibold text-text-primary hover:text-accent select-none list-none flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>View GST Slabs &amp; Split Structure</span>
                <span class="text-accent group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 pl-2">
                <p>• <strong>Primary Slabs:</strong> 0% (Exempt essentials), 5% (Merit goods/food), 18% (Standard commercial services/goods), 40% (Demerit luxury / vehicles >350cc).</p>
                <p>• <strong>Intrastate Billing:</strong> CGST = Tax ÷ 2, SGST/UTGST = Tax ÷ 2.</p>
                <p>• <strong>Interstate Billing:</strong> IGST = 100% of Tax amount.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </article>

          <!-- Formula: Income Tax 115BAC -->
          <article id="income-tax" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap">
              <div>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Taxation · Direct Tax</span>
                <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">
                  4. Indian Income Tax — Section 115BAC New Tax Regime
                </h3>
              </div>
              <a href="/in/income-tax-calculator" class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">
                Try Income Tax Calculator →
              </a>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Plain-Language Explanation:</strong> Under the statutory New Tax Regime (FY 2025-26 &amp; FY 2026-27), salaried taxpayers receive a ₹75,000 standard deduction. Full rebate under Section 87A is provided up to ₹12 Lakh taxable income. Together, salaried individuals earning up to <strong>₹12.75 Lakh pay ₹0 tax</strong>. If income slightly exceeds ₹12 Lakh, Section 87A marginal relief legally caps your tax liability so you never pay more tax than the excess income earned.
            </p>

            <div class="p-4 bg-canvas border border-border rounded-control text-xs font-mono space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto">
              <div class="text-accent font-bold">Taxable Income = Gross Salary − ₹75,000 Standard Deduction</div>
              <div>₹0 – ₹4,00,000: Nil (0%)</div>
              <div>₹4,00,001 – ₹8,00,000: 5% of amount over ₹4L</div>
              <div>₹8,00,001 – ₹12,00,000: ₹20,000 + 10% of amount over ₹8L</div>
              <div>₹12,00,001 – ₹16,00,000: ₹60,000 + 15% of amount over ₹12L</div>
              <div>₹16,00,001 – ₹20,00,000: ₹1,20,000 + 20% of amount over ₹16L</div>
              <div>₹20,00,001 – ₹24,00,000: ₹2,00,000 + 25% of amount over ₹20L</div>
              <div>Above ₹24,00,000: ₹3,00,000 + 30% of amount over ₹24L</div>
              <div class="text-text-muted pt-1 border-t border-border">Health &amp; Education Cess: 4% on net tax liability after rebate.</div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Formula: CAGR & WACC -->
          <article id="cagr" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap">
              <div>
